Here are the sources (in C) for PC Larn 12.0, in uuencoded ARC'ed
form.  To use it, uudecode it, transfer it to an IBM PC or
compatible, and deARC it using ARC, UNARC, or whatever your
favorite deARCing program happens to be.

This file came from the pub/larn directory on NOSC-COD.ARPA, as
the file LARN12ASRC.ARC.

If you don't receive this properly, send mail to me or to John D.
Woolverton (jdw@tybalt.caltech.edu, jdw@tybalt.uucp) (who
suggested that I post this), and we will try to mail this to you.
If possible, give an Arpanet address, or construct a path from
here to your machine, because our mailer is messed up.

